Icecast 2.5.0: start listeners instantly and answer HEAD on stream mounts.

Icecast 2.5 attaches a new listener, sends its headers and its burst only
from the mount's source loop, which waits up to 250ms for source data and
then sits a listener out for a pass after each stage. Listeners waited
0.3-0.9s for audio (Icecast-KH: ~0s). With these changes the headers and
burst go out in the same pass, 2-12ms after connecting.

HEAD on a stream mount answered 405, which failed directory and stream
checkers (Radio Garden and others). It now returns the stream's headers
and closes. HEAD on anything else still answers 405.

